1
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:06,820
This is Trigun.

2
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:33,860
guitar solo

3
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:43,397
H-h-hah...

4
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:46,080
H-h-hah... Well?

5
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:47,737
Aren't you gonna shoot me?

6
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:49,349
Where do I find your boss?

7
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,637
I was bought.

8
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:55,838
It wasn't my fault.

9
00:01:56,120 --> 00:02:00,708
The man I thought to be my father turned
out to be nothing more than an angel.

10
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:03,398
I don't know anything else, I swear.

11
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:12,674
Hey, it's dangerous to be too trusting.

12
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:16,116
What if I decided to get up
and shoot you in the back?

13
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:21,040
I'm not that trusting.

14
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:23,985
I kept my finger on the
trigger the whole time.

15
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:36,380
What now, Vash?

16
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:49,200
Routine report, date July Thou.

17
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:53,520
Two days after the incident
caused by a man named Monev,

18
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:55,938
tension still runs high in the city.

19
00:02:57,260 --> 00:03:01,495
The events that occurred there made
me realize something all over again.

20
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:06,631
It's an awareness which becomes obscured
as I keep regular contact with him.

21
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:16,980
That being the reason Vash the Stampede
is called the Humanoid Typhoon.

22
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:18,960
I still don't understand.

23
00:03:19,260 --> 00:03:22,940
Why is it that so much trouble
falls into this man's lap?

24
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:25,440
Last December,

25
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:29,700
four months ago, we, Meryl
Stryfe and Millie Thompson,

26
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:33,491
employees of the Bernardelli
Insurance Society main office,

27
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:35,420
were handed down our orders.

28
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:40,197
Our objective was to make
contact with Vash the Stampede,

29
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,877
a man wanted for 60 billion double dollars

30
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:45,520
under suspicion of
Class G property damage.

31
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:48,400
Upon locating this humanoid typhoon,

32
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:52,117
it was our mission to minimize any
trouble involving him and bring a quick

33
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:56,557
resolution to situations that had
already started what about bash and why?

34
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:57,470
Are you asking?

35
00:03:57,553 --> 00:03:59,697
Don't tell me you two
innocent looking things

36
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:02,197
are after that 60 billion
double dollar reward?

37
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:03,557
Oh, not at all.

38
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:06,137
Yeah, actually we're just
passing through here on business!

39
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:07,320
Business?

40
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:10,337
Well, I didn't exactly see him myself.

41
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:13,832
As far as I could tell, he was
gone from the city by dawn.

42
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:16,957
Last I heard, he was
headed out to the east.

43
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:19,099
Can you tell me any more about him?

44
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:20,500
Hmm, well,

45
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:25,380
he stands about 12 fields tall,
and he wields a huge weapon,

46
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:28,779
he's supposed to have a
mohawk, and nerves of steel.

47
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:31,937
Apparently, he's got tons of henchmen,

48
00:04:32,020 --> 00:04:35,491
and a reputation as the worst
womanizer anyone's ever seen.

49
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:37,790
Womanizer?

50
00:04:37,873 --> 00:04:38,955
I heard what he said.

51
00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:40,571
Huge weapon and a mohawk.

52
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:42,632
That's our man, alright.

53
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:47,077
Having obtained information of
someone matching Vash's description,

54
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:50,454
we finally achieved contact
with him after three months.

55
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:53,640
Now, what do you want?

56
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:55,620
I'm very pleased to meet you.

57
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:56,880
My name is Meryl.

58
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:58,270
I...

59
00:04:58,353 --> 00:05:02,537
I'm Meryl Stryfe, and I'm here representing
the Bernardelli Insurance Society.

60
00:05:02,620 --> 00:05:04,032
And I'm Millie Thompson!

61
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:07,340
This, uh, is a small
token of our goodwill.

62
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:09,340
Nice going, Meryl!

63
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:11,538
What are you doing?

64
00:05:11,940 --> 00:05:13,234
Are you here with him?

65
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:16,140
It was him.

66
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,540
The outlaw, Vash the Stampede.

67
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:22,297
That's a lot different from
what actually happened.

68
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:25,357
I took a little bit of license
to keep it interesting.

69
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:29,028
Come on, Millie, do you want to
get a promotion or don't you?

70
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:36,751
At first glance, I must admit, it was
a bit difficult to tell if it was him.

71
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:38,957
This was because he didn't
act anything like the

72
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:41,097
legendary gunman that
I've heard so much about.

73
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:44,417
In fact, the only thing legendary
about him was his huge appetite.

74
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:45,330
Okay, then, what?

75
00:05:45,413 --> 00:05:46,243
Stop!

76
00:05:46,340 --> 00:05:47,170
Just not!

77
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,920
No! Dang it!

78
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,150
Disgusting.

79
00:05:56,233 --> 00:05:57,063
Just ignore them.

80
00:05:57,146 --> 00:05:59,497
Hey, insurance girls! Snail, wait!

81
00:05:59,580 --> 00:06:00,677
Hey, where are you going?

82
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:01,760
I need your help!

83
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:04,018
How can you just leave me like this?

84
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:06,692
How about a little make-up kiss, brother?

85
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:12,869
He seemed to be nothing but a
vulgar, hopeless troublemaker.

86
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:24,360
And even worse yet, his incorrigible
lechery made him an exasperating idiot.

87
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,237
You can definitely count on me, Mr.

88
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:28,150
Cliff.

89
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:30,777
I don't let anyone in my sights get away,

90
00:06:30,860 --> 00:06:33,677
and I'm known for my bullets
never missing their mark.

91
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:35,937
especially if it's the
heart of a beautiful lady.

92
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:36,850
Bang!

93
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:40,276
Meryl, are you okay?

94
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:41,450
Uh?

95
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:47,717
Just remembering what happened
that day gives me chest pains.

96
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:49,837
I feel like my heart's
going to burst a vessel.

97
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:52,017
I thought Vash was really funny back then.

98
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,237
I laughed all the time.

99
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,357
What are you talking about?

100
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:55,270
He wasn't funny.

101
00:06:55,353 --> 00:06:56,497
He was downright weird.

102
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:59,217
Millie, nobody in their right mind
could tell that goofball was him.

103
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:00,537
How could you even think that?

104
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:02,177
But I thought it was him from the start.

105
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:04,177
You're the one who refused to believe it.

106
00:07:04,260 --> 00:07:07,617
Does it bother you that much
that I could be right about him?

107
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:09,957
Millie, have you finished
writing the papers yet?

108
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:11,760
No, but I'll keep at it.

109
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:19,137
He tried to fool us with his perfect
portrayal of a good-for-nothing,

110
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:20,050
dim-witted loser,

111
00:07:20,133 --> 00:07:24,497
but it soon became clear to me that his
antics were merely part of his little game.

112
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:27,397
I was able to confirm his
true identity as I watched

113
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:30,186
him resolve every incident
he was involved in.

114
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:31,730
Suicide?

115
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:36,522
To tell you the truth, I disapprove
of suicide more than anything.

116
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:39,520
All right, the boomerang it is.

117
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,190
What?

118
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:01,925
Dangerous toys are fun,
but you could get hurt.

119
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:04,060
You bastard!

120
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:08,500
Watch out!

121
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:16,090
Scary!

122
00:08:22,260 --> 00:08:23,090
Sam!

123
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:33,100
Just no skill.

124
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:37,260
What the hell are you, anyway?

125
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:41,476
I'm your bodyguard and ace
gunman, just as advertised.

126
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:45,724
What do you think you're doing?

127
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:48,760
Trying to play the hero,
cowboy? No, not really.

128
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:51,332
I'm not as great as you might think I am.

129
00:08:56,180 --> 00:08:59,037
Ah gee that's too bad
you've got a flat tire

130
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:01,649
well I guess you won't
be escaping in this!

131
00:09:18,740 --> 00:09:25,100
Are you crazy do you have any idea what
you're getting yourself into Mister?

132
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:29,717
This gentleman here is the one and
only infamous humanoid typhoon!

133
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:31,520
He's Vash the Stampede!

134
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:33,210
That's funny.

135
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:34,730
Pardon me.

136
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,297
But I was under the impression
that he was a lot more handsome.

137
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:41,262
Are you implying that I
am not Vash the Stampede?

138
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,320
Maybe we should find out.

139
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:49,997
He was a superb gunman,
just as the rumors claimed,

140
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:52,609
and every incident he
was in was swiftly...

141
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:53,830
swiftly...

142
00:09:53,913 --> 00:09:55,240
He did it so haphazardly.

143
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:59,478
How could those incidents have been
anything but dumb luck any of them

144
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:14,730
Still

145
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:18,337
Still it is the unmistakable truth that he

146
00:10:18,420 --> 00:10:20,637
solved each incident
without the use of his gun.

147
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:25,157
He absolutely refused to harm
anyone even when citizens?

148
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:27,597
tried to kill him to collect
the bounty of his head.

149
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:28,510
Ah!

150
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:29,940
Can this be the end?

151
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:34,280
There he is! In here! Oh, crap!

152
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:37,197
I killed you!

153
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:39,040
I killed you now!

154
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:41,960
Oh, really? Do you mean me?

155
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:49,330
Momma!

156
00:10:49,413 --> 00:10:50,337
Why does this keep happening to me?

157
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:51,417
I haven't done anything wrong,

158
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:53,717
but I'm always in trouble and
everybody's always picking on me.

159
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:54,918
What do I do, Momma?

160
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,900
Why am I crying in French?

161
00:10:58,740 --> 00:11:00,622
Why does he act the way he does?

162
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:03,737
I can only speculate, but
perhaps part of the reason?

163
00:11:03,820 --> 00:11:06,277
Can be found in the testimony
of Miss Monica Allen.

164
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,772
at the left of the city.

165
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:11,780
Only one person has to
die to save this city.

166
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:13,480
So please, Mr.

167
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:14,933
Vash, give yourself up.

168
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,460
Please don't move.

169
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:24,462
I understand your situation
better than you know.

170
00:11:26,340 --> 00:11:27,170
However...

171
00:11:27,253 --> 00:11:28,644
No, please, sir, don't do that.

172
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:34,580
Until I see this man you're after,
I have no choice but to keep moving.

173
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,320
Now, please.

174
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:43,020
Who do you think Mr.

175
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:46,964
Vash was referring to when he
mentioned the man Monica was after?

176
00:11:56,100 --> 00:11:58,840
And so he finally took
his gun into his hand.

177
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:02,077
He pulled the trigger
for the first time to

178
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:04,925
save the very people who
had tried to kill him.

179
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:24,680
Hey, time's up, Wonderboy!

180
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:27,568
Throw the fear of death
into him, Goofstuff!

181
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:33,977
How did you do that?

182
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:47,300
I can't believe you both
are still alive and well!

183
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:52,025
I was kinda hoping you'd ditch
the woman and save your own skin!

184
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:53,377
Vash wouldn't do that!

185
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:55,166
He isn't that kind of person!

186
00:12:56,060 --> 00:12:58,360
So you won't kill no matter what, huh?

187
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:01,160
You are disgusting!

188
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:03,177
You know what, Vess?

189
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:05,378
You're nothing but a damn hypocrite.

190
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:10,988
There's no way you haven't had to kill
troublemakers somewhere along the line.

191
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:12,700
How do I know?

192
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:17,469
Because nobody can survive what you've
been through without hurting somebody.

193
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:21,821
The $60 billion double dollar bounty
on your head is proof of that.

194
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:27,869
Well, what do you have to say
for yourself, Vestas Stampede?

195
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:47,107
You're finally ready to fight, are you?

196
00:13:47,190 --> 00:13:50,627
Oh, so you want to draw?

197
00:13:50,710 --> 00:13:52,207
You felt it, twice!

198
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:56,447
Already, even your puny brain can realize
my son's fist is a force to be reckoned.

199
00:13:56,530 --> 00:13:59,587
or do you really believe
you'll survive another one?

200
00:13:59,670 --> 00:14:01,690
This is your last chance to run!

201
00:14:01,870 --> 00:14:03,887
Although no matter how fast you are,

202
00:14:03,970 --> 00:14:07,617
within the next few minutes
you'll be smashing to tiny pieces!

203
00:14:07,970 --> 00:14:09,210
Now pay attention,

204
00:14:09,430 --> 00:14:11,147
because as a courtesy I'm going to lecture

205
00:14:11,230 --> 00:14:13,767
you on just what a stupid
fool you really are!

206
00:14:13,850 --> 00:14:15,085
Using this technique!

207
00:14:18,570 --> 00:14:21,230
A human mincemeat special course!

208
00:14:21,910 --> 00:14:23,230
Don't have to quit!

209
00:14:23,590 --> 00:14:27,825
Enjoy being a hero for a moment,
They've died in a most humiliating way.

210
00:15:22,370 --> 00:15:24,087
He did it!

211
00:15:24,170 --> 00:15:26,230
It changed course!

212
00:15:26,630 --> 00:15:27,890
That was great!

213
00:15:30,590 --> 00:15:34,810
It cost my son's fist to be off
course with six little bullets!

214
00:15:35,150 --> 00:15:36,070
Not quite, Doc.

215
00:15:38,230 --> 00:15:39,610
I have one left.

216
00:15:40,210 --> 00:15:41,850
Could be my special one.

217
00:16:04,730 --> 00:16:07,567
I can't believe it did
you see what he did you

218
00:16:07,650 --> 00:16:10,707
really beat him and he did
it with only six bullets,

219
00:16:10,790 --> 00:16:11,620
unbelievable!

220
00:16:14,650 --> 00:16:16,950
Suddenly it's become very clear to me

221
00:16:17,570 --> 00:16:19,805
why he is called the Humanoid Typhoon.

222
00:16:21,830 --> 00:16:23,771
It's actually him, he's for real,

223
00:16:24,470 --> 00:16:27,590
the legendary outlaw, Vash the Stampede.

224
00:16:29,210 --> 00:16:35,827
Oh yeah, no matter what, I think
this man is Vash the Stampede.

225
00:16:35,910 --> 00:16:39,310
Love and peace!

226
00:16:39,530 --> 00:16:41,470
Love and peace!

227
00:16:41,970 --> 00:16:44,287
Love and peace! Love and peace!

228
00:16:44,370 --> 00:16:46,090
Love and peace!

229
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:50,850
You're really fun to watch.

230
00:17:00,410 --> 00:17:02,410
Vash the Stampede.

231
00:17:03,070 --> 00:17:05,070
Every time I observe his actions,

232
00:17:05,450 --> 00:17:09,230
I can't help but sense something
hidden deep within him.

233
00:17:11,690 --> 00:17:13,984
Something we can't begin to understand.

234
00:17:30,390 --> 00:17:34,147
but this much is certain
everyone who has become involved

235
00:17:34,230 --> 00:17:37,910
with him has somehow regained
an emotion which was once lost.

236
00:17:38,550 --> 00:17:39,380
Father!

237
00:17:39,610 --> 00:17:40,728
Father, I'm coming!

238
00:17:41,210 --> 00:17:42,040
I'm...

239
00:17:42,123 --> 00:17:43,050
I'm all right, honey.

240
00:17:47,130 --> 00:17:48,630
This can't be happening.

241
00:17:49,230 --> 00:17:50,990
It was you all the time.

242
00:17:53,230 --> 00:17:55,730
Like I've mentioned so many times before,

243
00:17:56,410 --> 00:17:57,998
nothing beats Hardwon fame.

244
00:18:02,650 --> 00:18:06,787
From this point on, we're gonna go
on living without relying on anyone.

245
00:18:06,870 --> 00:18:08,517
It'll be just the two of us.

246
00:18:10,290 --> 00:18:12,408
That's nice of you guys to say that.

247
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:17,090
But I still wonder...

248
00:18:20,870 --> 00:18:21,890
Mr. Vash!

249
00:18:26,650 --> 00:18:27,480
Stay back!

250
00:18:30,010 --> 00:18:31,130
Stay away from me.

251
00:18:39,390 --> 00:18:40,467
Who is he?

252
00:18:40,550 --> 00:18:41,590
That's not Vash.

253
00:18:41,710 --> 00:18:42,827
That is not the same man.

254
00:18:42,910 --> 00:18:44,127
Who is that man?

255
00:18:44,210 --> 00:18:47,130
Can he possibly be the
real Vash the Stampede?

256
00:18:47,370 --> 00:18:52,252
The evil 60 billion double dollar outlaw
with the fire of hell burning in his eyes?

257
00:18:58,170 --> 00:19:00,930
You will pay, you will pay for this.

258
00:19:06,970 --> 00:19:08,050
They're dead.

259
00:19:08,870 --> 00:19:10,070
People are dead.

260
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:12,190
Who the hell cares?

261
00:19:15,970 --> 00:19:17,610
You killed all the people!

262
00:19:18,250 --> 00:19:20,721
They're all dead, and you killed them all!

263
00:19:22,130 --> 00:19:24,483
And you were the one solely responsible!

264
00:19:27,830 --> 00:19:29,690
Now it is your turn to die!

265
00:19:41,370 --> 00:19:43,194
There are so many sides to him.

266
00:19:43,630 --> 00:19:45,070
Which is the real Vash?

267
00:19:46,110 --> 00:19:47,470
I don't understand.

268
00:19:49,090 --> 00:19:49,920
Listen.

269
00:19:50,070 --> 00:19:51,350
We're all scared.

270
00:19:51,630 --> 00:19:53,070
We can't sleep at night.

271
00:19:53,330 --> 00:19:54,727
You're not the only one.

272
00:19:54,810 --> 00:19:57,747
Can't we get someone to tell
him to get out of this hotel?

273
00:19:57,830 --> 00:19:59,889
Don't bash the stampede to get out?

274
00:20:00,770 --> 00:20:01,790
Are you insane?

275
00:20:08,110 --> 00:20:09,730
Bash, are you all right?

276
00:20:28,230 --> 00:20:31,327
So those scars are the price you paid for

277
00:20:31,410 --> 00:20:34,292
dealing with your opponents
without killing them.

278
00:20:35,190 --> 00:20:38,330
It's not exactly something
I like girls to see.

279
00:20:38,690 --> 00:20:40,808
I think many of them would run away.

280
00:20:41,010 --> 00:20:42,186
I wouldn't run away.

281
00:20:42,590 --> 00:20:44,825
What I mean is they wouldn't run away.

282
00:20:45,390 --> 00:20:48,919
Uh, Vash, I've been meaning to
ask you this for a while now.

283
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:50,947
You haven't done anything wrong,

284
00:20:51,030 --> 00:20:53,407
yet terrible things keep
happening to you all the time.

285
00:20:53,490 --> 00:20:56,707
The townspeople look at you like
you're some sort of criminal.

286
00:20:56,790 --> 00:20:58,202
Doesn't that bother you?

287
00:21:00,810 --> 00:21:02,747
How can you go on living this way?

288
00:21:02,830 --> 00:21:03,990
It seems so awful.

289
00:21:04,330 --> 00:21:05,190
I can't.

290
00:21:05,530 --> 00:21:06,690
I can't do that.

291
00:21:07,250 --> 00:21:09,050
I haven't yet buried my past.

292
00:21:09,730 --> 00:21:11,367
There's no way I can live in peace?

293
00:21:11,450 --> 00:21:13,307
Until I've come to terms with it.

294
00:21:13,390 --> 00:21:15,802
and I'm able to finally put it behind me.

295
00:21:35,290 --> 00:21:36,120
You leaving?

296
00:21:36,870 --> 00:21:39,487
Hey, thanks, Sheriff, for
letting me go like this.

297
00:21:39,570 --> 00:21:42,307
I'm only doing it because I
don't want you in my town.

298
00:21:42,390 --> 00:21:43,287
And I don't want you.

299
00:21:43,370 --> 00:21:44,200
Thanks.

300
00:21:44,283 --> 00:21:45,967
I just want you to get the hell out.

301
00:21:46,050 --> 00:21:50,107
Yeah.

302
00:21:50,190 --> 00:21:56,527
I guess I Will do you plan

303
00:21:56,610 --> 00:21:57,767
to follow him this time?

304
00:21:57,850 --> 00:22:00,847
Course. I am. I have to.
It's my job. That's True.

305
00:22:00,930 --> 00:22:01,760
You're right.

306
00:22:01,843 --> 00:22:03,607
I can't very well leave the
two of you alone together.

307
00:22:03,690 --> 00:22:05,147
So I Suppose I better come along.

308
00:22:05,230 --> 00:22:08,227
Anyone ever tell you you're
just simply annoying?

309
00:22:08,310 --> 00:22:09,667
Oh Oh really?

310
00:22:09,750 --> 00:22:10,647
Young lady.

311
00:22:10,730 --> 00:22:13,847
When you travel all alone in the
desert it can be very perilous.

312
00:22:13,930 --> 00:22:17,347
But if you act now you can hire your
very own bodyguard free of charge.

313
00:22:17,430 --> 00:22:18,347
And my work is guaranteed.

314
00:22:18,430 --> 00:22:19,527
Oh? Great.

315
00:22:19,610 --> 00:22:21,967
I take my eyes off him for a
minute and he's at it again.

316
00:22:22,050 --> 00:22:22,880
Wait.

317
00:22:22,963 --> 00:22:23,793
Where are you going?

318
00:22:23,876 --> 00:22:24,706
Hey?

319
00:22:24,789 --> 00:22:25,619
Don't just walk away.

320
00:22:25,702 --> 00:22:26,532
Come on now.

321
00:22:26,615 --> 00:22:27,447
Young lady.

322
00:22:27,530 --> 00:22:29,830
Bash the stampede.

323
00:22:51,050 --> 00:22:52,367
Thank

324
00:22:52,450 --> 00:22:59,327
you so much

325
00:22:59,410 --> 00:23:06,410
for

326
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:09,320
watching.

327
00:23:09,403 --> 00:23:13,530
I'll just leave my left.

328
00:23:16,650 --> 00:23:23,447
When I'm looking at my eyes
and I'm looking at my eyes!

329
00:23:23,530 --> 00:23:27,530
I don't need anything else.

330
00:23:56,110 --> 00:23:57,510
Yeah?

331
00:24:07,630 --> 00:24:11,107
If you only face forward, there
is something you will miss seeing.

332
00:24:11,190 --> 00:24:16,131
It is a virtue to devote oneself to something,
firmly believing in one's own ideals.

333
00:24:16,510 --> 00:24:20,867
But that does not mean it's alright to
belittle the ideals or feelings of others.

334
00:24:20,950 --> 00:24:24,667
If you lead such a busy life, and you
don't realize how your parents feel,

335
00:24:24,750 --> 00:24:29,547
it's only self-satisfaction it's all
right to stop every now and again

336
00:24:29,630 --> 00:24:35,010
if you want a moment's rest if you
want to feel what other people feel
